  "body": "Some homes are renovated. Others are completely reimagined.\r\n\r\nThis exceptional 264m2 (approx) Mairangi Bay residence belongs firmly in the latter category. It has been transformed with an uncompromising eye for quality, craftsmanship and detail-with no stone left unturned.\r\n\r\nFrom the moment you enter, the difference is unmistakable. A dramatic feature entrance, bespoke wall treatments and carefully considered lighting set the tone, while the statement kitchen combines striking design with genuine functionality. Premium appliances, induction cooking and a full butler's pantry make it equally suited to everyday family life and effortless entertaining.\r\n\r\nThe scale is impressive-and importantly, the floor area is devoted to living. With a streamlined single internal-access garage rather than garaging dominating the footprint, there is almost another room's worth of usable internal space compared with many similarly sized homes.\r\n\r\nFour generous bedrooms, three beautifully appointed bathrooms plus a powder room, and two distinct living areas provide genuine flexibility for families of all ages. Even the powder room is concealed behind a disappearing door-one of many clever details waiting to be discovered.\r\n\r\nThe main living area flows seamlessly onto a covered entertainer's deck, creating a sophisticated extension of the home that can be enjoyed throughout the seasons. Beyond it, immaculate landscaping, sensor-lit pathways and a private mini-putt garden continue the sense that absolutely nothing has been overlooked.\r\n\r\nElevated above its surroundings, the home enjoys a sweeping urban outlook with a glimpse across Mairangi Bay to the sea. Its sheltered inland position delivers the best of the Bays lifestyle while remaining comfortably removed from the direct coastal edge.\r\n\r\nMairangi Bay Village, the beach and exceptional schooling are all within easy reach, with zoning for Mairangi Bay School, Murrays Bay Intermediate and Rangitoto College.\r\n\r\nWHY YOU'LL LOVE IT:\r\n\r\n* An impressive 264m², with more floor area devoted to genuine living\r\n* Four generous bedrooms and two separate living areas\r\n* Three luxurious bathrooms plus a cleverly concealed powder room\r\n* Statement kitchen with induction cooking and full butler's pantry\r\n* Bespoke finishes, feature walls and carefully considered lighting\r\n* Covered all-season entertainer's deck\r\n* Immaculately landscaped grounds with private mini-putt garden\r\n* Elevated urban outlook with a glimpse of the sea\r\n* Single internal-access garage plus additional off-street parking\r\n* Sensor-lit driveway and pathways\r\n* Sheltered inland position close to Mairangi Bay Village and the beach\r\n* Zoned for Mairangi Bay School, Murrays Bay Intermediate and Rangitoto College\r\n\r\nThis is not simply a home where the work has been completed. It is a home where every decision has been made with purpose, every detail has been considered and quality can be felt at every turn.\r\n\r\nBeautiful, individual and virtually impossible to replicate-this is Mairangi Bay living at an entirely different level.\r\n\r\nAUCTION: Thursday 3 December 2026 from 5pm at Ray White Milford (Unless Sold Prior)\r\nINFO: rwmairangibay.co.nz/MRG32534 (scroll down to documents)",
